  "name": "rust-ttt",
  "description": "An implementation of the Tic-Tac-Toe game engine in early-dialect Rust, featuring a modular architecture that decouples core game logic from terminal-based I/O. The system employs a recursive Minimax algorithm for optimal adversarial search, supporting automated player decision-making and various human-agent interaction modes. Architectural robustness is maintained through polymorphic reader and writer abstractions, facilitating comprehensive unit testing of board state transitions and AI heuristics.",
